module vid-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6-virgin-islands }

// The District Court of the Virgin Islands' own civil periods, computed
// under the federal rules (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"; LRCi 6.1(a)
// adds to "legal holiday" any day on which both divisions of the court are
// closed). Motions under Rules 12 and 56 are filed within the FRCP
// deadlines or as a court order sets (LRCi 6.1(b)(1)(i)), so they belong
// to lit/frcp. Absent an order setting deadlines, and except for motions
// in limine, the parties may negotiate one extension of a motion, response
// or reply deadline, of at most 30 days from the deadline the rule sets,
// on notice filed before the original filing date (LRCi 6.1(b)(5)); it
// extends a period and declares none of its own, so it stays in this note.
// A non-dispositive motion represents that consent was sought at least 24
// hours before filing (LRCi 7.1(e)); the corpus counts no hours, so it
// stays in this note. Three periods are counted in business days, which
// FRCP 6(a) does not define: the initial pretrial memorandum, no less than
// three business days before the initial Rule 16 scheduling conference
// (LRCi 16.1(a)); depositions eligible for filing, at least three business
// days before trial (LRCi 30.1(e)); and proposed trial exhibits, in
// electronic form at least three business days before the first day of
// trial (LRCi 39.1(a)); they stay in this note. A de bene esse deposition
// solely to authenticate records may be taken after the discovery deadline
// without leave only more than 28 days before trial (LRCi 26.4(a)); an
// expert whose testimony was not video-taped and who is unavailable does
// not delay a trial set at least 45 days in advance (LRCi 26.3(c)); motions
// to compel are filed within the discovery period (LRCi 26.5); the
// judgment creditor files a garnishment receipt every three months after
// serving the levy (LRCi 69.1(d)(1)). These are conditions, not deadlines
// from an event, so they stay in this note. Review of the clerk's taxation
// of costs by motion served within seven days of the clerk's action (LRCi
// 54.1(d)) is FRCP 54(d)(1)'s period and belongs to lit/frcp. A civil
// cover sheet is not required of a pro se filer (LRCi 3.1(c)). Rules that
// state no period or limit stay out. The earlier D.V.I. outline's FRCP
// flow and its decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Phillips v. County of Allegheny,
// Fowler v. UPMC Shadyside, Goines, Foman v. Davis, Frow v. De La Vega,
// Poulis v. State Farm, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Catlin, Bowles
// v. Russell) are FRCP or FRAP authority and belong to lit/frcp and
// lit/frap; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A motion, response or reply: at most the greater of 20 pages or 6,000
/// words, excluding exhibits, supporting documentation, the caption, the
/// signature block and certificates, without leave of Court; a filing over
/// 20 substantive pages carries a word-count certificate, and leave granted
/// to the movant gives the respondent an equal extension (D.V.I. LRCi
/// 7.1(b)).
limit motion-paper {
  pages <= 20 cite "D.V.I. LRCi 7.1(b)"
  words <= 6_000 cite "D.V.I. LRCi 7.1(b)"
} cite "D.V.I. LRCi 7.1(b)"

/// The Clerk gives notice that a complaint was filed without a completed
/// civil cover sheet (D.V.I. LRCi 3.1(b)).
event CoverSheetOmissionNoticed()
/// The hearing on a motion to withdraw as counsel for an individual
/// (D.V.I. LRCi 5.2(b)).
event WithdrawalHearing()
/// The Court enters the order or decision of which reconsideration is
/// sought (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(1)(ii)).
event OrderEntered()
/// The day scheduled for jury selection (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(1)(iii)).
event JurySelection()
/// A motion is served (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(2)).
event MotionServed() paper motion-paper
/// A response to a motion is served (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(2)).
event ResponseServed() paper motion-paper
/// A Rule 12 motion is filed (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(i)).
event Rule12MotionFiled() paper motion-paper
/// A response to a Rule 12 motion is filed (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(i)).
event Rule12ResponseFiled() paper motion-paper
/// A Rule 56 motion for summary judgment is filed
/// (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(ii)).
event SummaryJudgmentMotionFiled() paper motion-paper
/// A response to a Rule 56 motion is filed (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(ii)).
event SummaryJudgmentResponseFiled() paper motion-paper
/// A motion for reconsideration is served (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(iii)).
event ReconsiderationMotionServed() paper motion-paper
/// A response to a motion for reconsideration is filed
/// (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(iii)).
event ReconsiderationResponseFiled() paper motion-paper
/// A motion in limine is filed (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(iv)).
event LimineMotionFiled() paper motion-paper
/// A response to a motion in limine is filed (D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(iv)).
event LimineResponseFiled() paper motion-paper
/// A motion, response or reply over the page and word limit is filed
/// (D.V.I. LRCi 7.1(b)).
event OversizePaperFiled() paper motion-paper
/// The date set for trial (D.V.I. LRCi 16.1(c)).
event TrialDate()
/// An expert witness's deposition (D.V.I. LRCi 26.3(d)).
event ExpertDeposition()
/// The deposition of an individual (D.V.I. LRCi 30.1(a)).
event IndividualDeposition()
/// The deposition of an organization under FRCP 30(b)(6)
/// (D.V.I. LRCi 30.1(a)).
event OrganizationDeposition()
/// Notice of an FRCP 30(b)(6) deposition is served (D.V.I. LRCi 30.1(b)).
event OrganizationDepositionNoticeServed()
/// The moving party serves a written communication requesting the
/// discovery conference of counsel (D.V.I. LRCi 37.1(b)).
event DiscoveryConferenceRequested()
/// The offering party receives the Clerk's written request to claim
/// exhibits (D.V.I. LRCi 39.1(d)).
event ExhibitClaimRequestReceived()
/// An interpreter's services are required at an in-court proceeding
/// (D.V.I. LRCi 43.1).
event InterpreterNeeded()
/// A final judgment, or a judgment allowing costs, is entered
/// (D.V.I. LRCi 54.1(a)).
event CostsJudgmentEntered()
/// A wage garnishment levy is satisfied (D.V.I. LRCi 69.1(d)).
event LevySatisfied()

/// D.V.I. LRCi 3.1(b): if the outstanding civil cover sheet is not filed
/// within three days of the Clerk's notice of the omission, the Court may
/// dismiss the action.
deadline cover-sheet-period: 3.days after CoverSheetOmissionNoticed() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 3.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 5.2(b)(1): a request by an individual whose counsel moves
/// to withdraw to appear at the hearing by video or teleconference is made
/// by motion at least three days before the hearing.
deadline withdrawal-remote-appearance-period: 3.days before WithdrawalHearing() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 5.2(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(1)(ii) and 7.3(a): a motion for reconsideration is
/// filed within 14 days after entry of the order or decision, unless the
/// Court extends the time for good cause.
deadline reconsideration-motion-period: 14.days after OrderEntered() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(1)(iii): motions in limine are filed no later than
/// 28 days before the day scheduled for jury selection, or as the Court
/// directs.
deadline limine-motion-period: 28.days before JurySelection() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(2): except as LRCi 6.1(b)(3) or an order provides, a
/// response is filed within 14 days after service of a motion; the Court
/// may shorten or extend the time.
deadline response-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(2): a reply, if any, is filed within seven days
/// after service of the response.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(i): a response to a Rule 12 motion is filed
/// within 21 days of the filing of the motion.
deadline rule12-response-period: 21.days after Rule12MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(i): a reply on a Rule 12 motion is filed within
/// 14 days of the filing of the response.
deadline rule12-reply-period: 14.days after Rule12ResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(ii): a response to a Rule 56 motion, with
/// affidavits and supporting documents, may be filed within 21 days of the
/// filing of the motion.
deadline summary-judgment-response-period: 21.days after SummaryJudgmentMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(ii): a reply on a Rule 56 motion is filed within
/// 14 days of the filing of the response.
deadline summary-judgment-reply-period: 14.days after SummaryJudgmentResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(iii): a response to a motion for reconsideration
/// may be filed within 14 days after service of the motion.
deadline reconsideration-response-period: 14.days after ReconsiderationMotionServed() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(iii): a reply on a motion for reconsideration is
/// filed within seven days of the filing of the response.
deadline reconsideration-reply-period: 7.days after ReconsiderationResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(iv): a response to a motion in limine is filed
/// within seven days of the filing of the motion.
deadline limine-response-period: 7.days after LimineMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)(3)(iv): a reply on a motion in limine is filed
/// within seven days of the filing of the response.
deadline limine-reply-period: 7.days after LimineResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 7.1(b)(1): leave to exceed the page or word limit is
/// sought at least two days before the filing of the document.
deadline oversize-leave-period: 2.days before OversizePaperFiled() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 7.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 16.1(c): no later than seven days before the date set for
/// trial, or as the Court directs, each party files a trial brief and, in
/// a jury case, requests to charge or, in a non-jury case, proposed
/// findings of fact and conclusions of law.
deadline trial-brief-period: 7.days before TrialDate() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 16.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 26.3(d)(1): unless the Court provides otherwise, a proposed
/// bill for the expert's charges is provided to the party seeking
/// discovery 20 days before the deposition.
deadline expert-bill-period: 20.days before ExpertDeposition() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 26.3(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 30.1(a): "reasonable written notice" under FRCP 30(b)(1)
/// is at least 14 days before the deposition of an individual.
deadline individual-deposition-notice-period: 14.days before IndividualDeposition() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 30.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 30.1(a): "reasonable written notice" under FRCP 30(b)(1)
/// is at least 21 days before the deposition of an organization under FRCP
/// 30(b)(6).
deadline organization-deposition-notice-period: 21.days before OrganizationDeposition() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 30.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 30.1(b): the party taking an FRCP 30(b)(6) deposition
/// initiates and conducts the conference on the matters for examination
/// at least five days before service of the notice of deposition.
deadline organization-deposition-conference-period: 5.days before OrganizationDepositionNoticeServed() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 30.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 37.1(b): unless a stipulation or order provides otherwise,
/// the conference of counsel before a discovery motion is completed within
/// 15 calendar days after the moving party serves its written request for
/// the conference.
deadline discovery-conference-period: 15.days after DiscoveryConferenceRequested() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 37.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 39.1(d): the offering party claims its exhibits from the
/// Clerk within thirty days of receipt of the Clerk's written request;
/// unclaimed exhibits may be destroyed or otherwise disposed of.
deadline exhibit-claim-period: 30.days after ExhibitClaimRequestReceived() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 39.1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 43.1: the parties submit the names and qualifications of
/// qualified interpreters for approval at least six days before the
/// interpreter's services are required.
deadline interpreter-submission-period: 6.days before InterpreterNeeded() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 43.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 54.1(a): within 14 days after entry of a final judgment or
/// a judgment allowing costs, the prevailing party serves and files a Bill
/// of Costs.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after CostsJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 54.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCi 69.1(d)(4): the judgment creditor moves to vacate a wage
/// levy within 20 days after it has been satisfied.
deadline levy-vacatur-period: 20.days after LevySatisfied() counted_by frcp6-virgin-islands cite "D.V.I. LRCi 69.1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}
